Package: fabos-ai
Version: @DISTRO_VERSION@-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @VENDOR_NAME@ <support@patienceai.in>
Depends: systemd, libc6, llama.cpp, llama.cpp-tools, curl, python3
Description: @DISTRO_NAME@ AI stack — built-in offline model, intents, agents, governor, provenance, rollback
 The local-first AI service (aiosd) and CLI (aios) from the ai-native-os
 project. AI proposes, deterministic policy verifies, the kernel enforces,
 provenance records, transactions allow rollback. Cloud providers are off
 until the user adds a key. Enabling the user service is "System-Wide AI = ON":
   systemctl --user enable --now aiosd
 .
 Also serves the built-in offline model that ships inside every @DISTRO_NAME@
 image (/usr/share/fabos/models, manifest /usr/share/fabos/ai-models.json)
 on demand: fabos-llama.socket listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 (the chat-completions
 API the agent already speaks), the first request starts llama-server, ten
 idle minutes unload it again.
 Needs 4 GB RAM. `fabos-local-model status` reports readiness as JSON.
